'''Wellig Yuns''' was a [[human]] [[Jedi Knight]]<ref name="Night AD">{{Acolyte|Night}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> lived during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=day-trivia-gallery-the-acolyte|text="Day" Trivia Gallery &#124; The Acolyte}} {{C|Slide 5}}</ref> In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> Yuns was briefed by [[Jedi Knight]] [[Yord Fandar]] on a [[Mission to Khofar|mission]] to [[Khofar]] to locate secluded [[Jedi Master]] [[Kelnacca]].<ref name="Day" />

While hiking through the forests of Khofar, Yuns stated that they had lost track of their [[Tynnan]] tracker, [[Bazil]]. However, the team eventually reached [[Kelnacca's shelter]] as night began to fall and demanded the surrender of anyone inside. Unbeknownst to them, a mysterious [[The Stranger|stranger]] approached them from behind. Yuns ignited their [[lightsaber]] in response to the Stranger drawing his [[The Stranger's lightsaber|blade]]. Charging him, Yuns was flung back by a powerful [[Force push]]. In the ensuing battle, Yuns was the first to be slain by the Stranger. Their corpse was then found by a disoriented and startled [[Verosha Aniseya|Osha]].<ref name="Night">{{Acolyte|Night}}</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Equipment==
Wellig Yuns wore brown [[Jedi apparel]] with gold accents, and wielded a [[lightsaber]] with a [[Color|green]] blade.<ref name="Day" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Jedi, albeit unidentified, first appeared in "[[Day (episode)|Day]],"<ref name="Day" /> the fourth episode of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', which premiered [[June 18]], [[2024]].<ref name="EPG">{{SW|url=series/the-acolyte/season-1-episode-4-day-episode-guide|text="Day" Episode Guide &#124; The Acolyte}}</ref>  Jedi was later identified as Wellig Yuns in the reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]''.<ref name="TVG" />

